{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1436605-so-you-want-to-be-an-alchemist","id":1436605,"title":"So you want to be an Alchemist?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-02-22T18:17:11-08:00","id":1436605,"title":"So you want to be an Alchemist?","content":"This touches on something I have long thought about and the recent post about magic enlightenment drugs brought it to mind once again. What does alchemy do? Creation has alchemy. It mentions mortals doing it and flat out calls them alchemists. It shows up in things like the White Elixer making vampires. It is one of the paths to sorcery. What is alchemy then? Is it just drugs? What about the transmutation of metals? If you use mystical mirrors to use sunlight on gold to get Orichalcum is that a kind of alchemy? The Yennin with their children made with 10 fathers talk about a formula so is that a kind of it? Is Craft: Alchemy a thing? What are its limits? Is it just fancy named chemistry or more in a setting like Exalted? Does it make the world too mystical and magical?<br /> <br /> Plenty of games and fiction and stuff from our own wold that certainly could fit into Exalted it seems have their own stuff that works too. The Witcher books and games, Taoist Alchemy, Atelier series of video games, Weapons of the Gods game, numerous manga, and plenty more all take the idea to different degrees. Game of Thrones, one of the listed suggested materials for Exalted inspiration even uses alchemy to make its Wildfire.<br /> <br /> I ask about all this not only because I am honestly curious what people think, but because the setting seems to include it without any definition. I also think the idea expands Creation to make it something more. If alchemy is a thing across Creation and not just these weird random pop ups it can become elements of stories. Merchants trade in strange reagents and we know why they would want them and why it is valuable. Artifact making gets more interesting because now you have more you can raise up to that level just like you have artifact swords as the step up from just a steel sword.<br /> <br /> So yeah. What do you think alchemy is in Exalted? What can it do? What can't it do? What should or shouldn't it do?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/BogMod\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/BogMod</a> I play a lot of videogames.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/131-bogmod","name":"BogMod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar131_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-22T19:22:25-08:00","id":1436614,"title":"","content":"For me Alchemy and thaumaturgy blend together in Exalted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/854-light-hero","name":"light-hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar854_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-22T19:22:29-08:00","id":1436615,"title":"","content":"My assumption is two parts alchemy being the old-timey word for chemistry, one part the kinds of things chemists thought might be possible back when it was called alchemy. With the latter trending towards higher difficulty than the former.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-23T01:30:42-08:00","id":1436654,"title":"","content":"I'll say what I've said elsewhere; if the game is going to introduce something like alchemy, it's irresponsible to do so in a manner so piecemeal that a thread such as this becomes necessary.<br /> <br /> Also weird to introduce the idea that the capacity to transmute things, but maybe only if you include something like magical materials into the mix (?), functions as a mundane craft in the Hundred Devils entry for bats.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-23T11:04:29-08:00","id":1436702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1436605-so-you-want-to-be-an-alchemist?p=1436654#post1436654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also weird to introduce the idea that the capacity to transmute things, but maybe only if you include something like magical materials into the mix (?), functions as a mundane craft in the Hundred Devils entry for bats.</div> </div> </div> </div>The transmutation of things is one of the classic goals of alchemy. Turning things from their base into their pure form. The whole lead into gold for example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/BogMod\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/BogMod</a> I play a lot of videogames.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/131-bogmod","name":"BogMod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar131_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-23T12:36:10-08:00","id":1436721,"title":"","content":"Transmutation of metals I think should be a thaumaturgic ritual but that\u2019s the exception, not the rule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-23T19:45:48-08:00","id":1436744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1436605-so-you-want-to-be-an-alchemist?p=1436721#post1436721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Transmutation of metals I think should be a thaumaturgic ritual but that\u2019s the exception, not the rule.</div> </div> </div> </div>What craft skill would you require for a roll for someone who wanted to turn gold into Orichalcum with special sunlight reflecting mirrors? Or do you think that example from the Core should be a special thaumaturgic ritual?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/BogMod\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/BogMod</a> I play a lot of videogames.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/131-bogmod","name":"BogMod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar131_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-24T03:04:53-08:00","id":1436770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BogMod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1436605-so-you-want-to-be-an-alchemist?p=1436702#post1436702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The transmutation of things is one of the classic goals of alchemy. Turning things from their base into their pure form. The whole lead into gold for example.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm quite sure Isator was commenting not on the transmutation itself, but on <i>where</i> it was mentioned.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><i>The difference between fiction and reality? Fiction has to make sense.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/434-astralporing","name":"Astralporing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar434_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-24T03:22:55-08:00","id":1436774,"title":"","content":"I always assume Alchemy is the &quot;potions&quot; skill, but Exalted is really against magic potions (that one sorcerous initiation aside), which feels like a fertile ground left untouched. There's a handful of magic drugs in the book (see ghosts, prophylactic, antidote), but i think the devs were really against DnD style Potion of Water Breathing or Potion of Stoneskin. Which is a shame, because those things are awesome, and it's kinda just kicked over to &quot;do a Working, the rules of which are vague by design and almost certainly include a unintended side effect&quot;. <br /> <br /> On the subject of Gold into Oricaclum, I think the same logic holds: we don't want rules for this because we don't want you doing it lightly (see: every artifact craft thread). Its supposed to be a Special Adventure designed by your ST.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-24T08:30:46-08:00","id":1436811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1436605-so-you-want-to-be-an-alchemist?p=1436774#post1436774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always assume Alchemy is the &quot;potions&quot; skill, but Exalted is really against magic potions (that one sorcerous initiation aside), which feels like a fertile ground left untouched. There's a handful of magic drugs in the book (see ghosts, prophylactic, antidote), but i think the devs were really against DnD style Potion of Water Breathing or Potion of Stoneskin. Which is a shame, because those things are awesome, and it's kinda just kicked over to &quot;do a Working, the rules of which are vague by design and almost certainly include a unintended side effect&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure that the Unintended Side Effect of your Water Breathing Working being that you have to drink a potion to turn it on for a scene is perfectly valid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-24T10:07:35-08:00","id":1436830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BogMod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1436605-so-you-want-to-be-an-alchemist?p=1436702#post1436702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The transmutation of things is one of the classic goals of alchemy. Turning things from their base into their pure form. The whole lead into gold for example.</div> </div> </div> </div>Setting aside the whole subject of how the goals of alchemy were primarily spiritual (transmuting lead into gold being intended as something that would correspond directly to an inner transformation of the self), the... full sentence that you just quoted was talking about the oddity of transmutation (in the more nondescript form of &quot;change one thing into another&quot;) as an apparently mundane craft.<br /> <br /> In addition to the matter of it being a tangential space to introduce it.<br /> <br /> If it's going to be a thing, it requires more attention, because the implications are significant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-24T22:52:22-08:00","id":1436940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1436605-so-you-want-to-be-an-alchemist?p=1436830#post1436830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Setting aside the whole subject of how the goals of alchemy were primarily spiritual (transmuting lead into gold being intended as something that would correspond directly to an inner transformation of the self), the... full sentence that you just quoted was talking about the oddity of transmutation (in the more nondescript form of &quot;change one thing into another&quot;) as an apparently mundane craft.<br /> <br /> In addition to the matter of it being a tangential space to introduce it.<br /> <br /> If it's going to be a thing, it requires more attention, because the implications are significant.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I definitely agree on the matter that it should get more attention. Of course part of the point of the thread as it is a thing that is referenced in different places in the 3e materials. As for the part about transmutation reading back I see I misunderstood what you were going with in that response. As for the aspect of how mundane it would be I suppose to me it would always kind of fall into the same zone as other crafts. You have mundane things which do limited stuff and then you have the next...tier? Like if you are armoror you can pick up craft artifact and make fancy armor. Presumably you could have your craft alchemy and then craft artifact to do really fancy stuff?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/BogMod\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/BogMod</a> I play a lot of videogames.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/131-bogmod","name":"BogMod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar131_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-25T01:57:40-08:00","id":1436959,"title":"","content":"I'd be inclined to let &quot;Craft: Alchemy&quot; just be &quot;Craft: Chemistry&quot;, and allow you to build alchemical wonders (like a Philospher's Stone) with &quot;Craft: Artifact&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-25T03:10:03-08:00","id":1436967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1436605-so-you-want-to-be-an-alchemist?p=1436959#post1436959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd be inclined to let &quot;Craft: Alchemy&quot; just be &quot;Craft: Chemistry&quot;, and allow you to build alchemical wonders (like a Philospher's Stone) with &quot;Craft: Artifact&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Chemistry part of alchemy definitely is a craft specialty. Creating some magical stuff indeed seems like Craft: Artifact. On the other hand, stuff like transmutations seem to me to lie more in the province of Occult than Craft.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><i>The difference between fiction and reality? Fiction has to make sense.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/434-astralporing","name":"Astralporing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar434_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-25T03:48:42-08:00","id":1436969,"title":"","content":"See I wouldn't allow mundane (Basic/Major project) alchemy any transformations (outside of chemical reactions). It's a fancy name for &quot;Craft: Pharmacology&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-25T04:41:50-08:00","id":1436973,"title":"","content":"Hmm, now I'm thinking about the idea that guano mixed with powdered red jade plus a few other reagents as a substitute for firedust is something that would make sense as not even a literal transmutation and just being a combustible mixture.<br /> <br /> Which only further complicates and obscures what the parameters of the Craft are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-25T06:12:02-08:00","id":1436984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1436605-so-you-want-to-be-an-alchemist?p=1436973#post1436973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, now I'm thinking about the idea that guano mixed with powdered red jade plus a few other reagents as a substitute for firedust is something that would make sense as not even a literal transmutation and just being a combustible mixture.<br /> <br /> Which only further complicates and obscures what the parameters of the Craft are.</div> </div> </div> </div>Firedust isn't magical. I'd let a player make a firedust substitute with Craft: Alchemy. (I think Scroll of Kings offered another firedust substitute made of pine oil.)<br /> <br /> I wouldn't let a player turn lead into gold (without Craft: Artifact or a Working). But I'd let them make Five Bounties Paste as a Major Project <br /> <br /> I wouldn't let a player make a tincture that separated the good and evil parts of their soul (without Craft: Artifact or a Working). But I'd let them brew a tonic that let's them see ghosts as a Major Project.<br /> <br /> I'd let them make a varnish that harderns Ironwood. Or a reagent that makes feathersteel. Or a luck potion that works as a talisman. I'd let them cook meth. YMMV.<br /> <br /> I would have Craft: Alchemy be an appropriate Means for alchemical workings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-25T06:20:38-08:00","id":1436985,"title":"","content":"Well, <i>alchemical reagents</i> were often mentioned in the core as an alternative to firedust for use in places not South, so yeah, just <i>ignore</i> that they call the result &quot;firedust&quot;.<br /> <br /> It's nice to have a rules reference for making such a thing, even if we only got it as &quot;there's no gunpowder allowed but ...&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-26T16:25:38-08:00","id":1437160,"title":"","content":"So this is kinda what I said already but I said it really unclearly so<br /> <br /> 1. Treat \u201calchemy\u201d as just an antiquated word for chemistry.<br /> <br /> 2. Note that Creation has an arbitrarily wide variety of quasi-magical chemicals with strange and miraculous properties.<br /> <br /> 3. Consider that, even when not getting fictional reactants involved, there\u2019s nothing but precedent for saying that many of the things early- and pre-modern alchemists/chemists thought possible that aren\u2019t possible IRL should be possible in Creation.<br /> <br /> Upshot? Most of what you mentioned or were thinking of in the OP should be fair game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-27T17:58:37-08:00","id":1437307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1436605-so-you-want-to-be-an-alchemist?p=1436984#post1436984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Firedust isn't magical. I'd let a player make a firedust substitute with Craft: Alchemy. (I think Scroll of Kings offered another firedust substitute made of pine oil.)<br /> <br /> I wouldn't let a player turn lead into gold (without Craft: Artifact or a Working). But I'd let them make Five Bounties Paste as a Major Project<br /> <br /> I wouldn't let a player make a tincture that separated the good and evil parts of their soul (without Craft: Artifact or a Working). But I'd let them brew a tonic that let's them see ghosts as a Major Project.<br /> <br /> I'd let them make a varnish that harderns Ironwood. Or a reagent that makes feathersteel. Or a luck potion that works as a talisman. I'd let them cook meth. YMMV.<br /> <br /> I would have Craft: Alchemy be an appropriate Means for alchemical workings.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Perhaps a question would be what would you think would clearly not be alchemy then? Beyond where some other craft clearly did the job. Like sure you could, to use your example, make feathersteel with alchemy but you are going to need blacksmithing or weaponsmithing to make a weapon out of the steel you made. Alchemy in a lot of settings gets used to create or manipulate life and we sort of see at least the later with how Volivats alchemists make superfood. If you have some fantasy setting and find some artificial humanoid or creature being grown in a tube it is probably alchemy. Speaking of workings though that does remind me on what exactly should Sorcery be able to do that sufficient Craft can't?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/BogMod\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/BogMod</a> I play a lot of videogames.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/131-bogmod","name":"BogMod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar131_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-28T01:03:31-08:00","id":1437330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BogMod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1436605-so-you-want-to-be-an-alchemist?p=1437307#post1437307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Perhaps a question would be what would you think would clearly not be alchemy then? Beyond where some other craft clearly did the job. Like sure you could, to use your example, make feathersteel with alchemy but you are going to need blacksmithing or weaponsmithing to make a weapon out of the steel you made. Alchemy in a lot of settings gets used to create or manipulate life and we sort of see at least the later with how Volivats alchemists make superfood. If you have some fantasy setting and find some artificial humanoid or creature being grown in a tube it is probably alchemy. Speaking of workings though that does remind me on what exactly should Sorcery be able to do that sufficient Craft can't?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think there is a clear delineation in crafts. Two of the sample crafts in the Core are Carpentry and Woodworking.<br /> <br /> I'd let you build a firewand with Craft Weapons. Or Craft Mechanical Devices. Or Craft Firedust Applications. I'd let you build an ironwood firewand with Craft Woodworking. I'd let you build a Dragon Sigh Wand with Craft Artifact and Craft Jadecarving.<br /> <br /> Same for Craft and Sorcerery.<br /> <br /> My Twilight is building an artifact hand. My Earth Aspect is using a Working to restore a lost limb.<br /> <br /> Different means can reach the same ends.<br /> <br /> Making life in a tube is probably Craft Alchemy and Craft First Age Artifice. But I'd let folks use something like Craft Genesis/Fleshcrafting/Horticulture/Simulacrum instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-28T18:53:05-08:00","id":1437411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1436605-so-you-want-to-be-an-alchemist?p=1436654#post1436654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll say what I've said elsewhere; if the game is going to introduce something like alchemy, it's irresponsible to do so in a manner so piecemeal that a thread such as this becomes necessary.<br /> <br /> Also weird to introduce the idea that the capacity to transmute things, but maybe only if you include something like magical materials into the mix (?), functions as a mundane craft in the Hundred Devils entry for bats.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait. Bats? Where's that one? <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/280914/Hundred-Devils-Night-Parade-Anuhle-the-Demon-Spider-and-Bat\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...Spider-and-Bat</a><br /> <br /> this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-28T22:11:21-08:00","id":1437422,"title":"","content":"I am also curious about the bats.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/BogMod\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/BogMod</a> I play a lot of videogames.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/131-bogmod","name":"BogMod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar131_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-28T23:03:09-08:00","id":1437428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BogMod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1436605-so-you-want-to-be-an-alchemist?p=1437422#post1437422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am also curious about the bats.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok. A friend of mine got a screenshot. No need to spend money.<br /> <br /> It appears that you can use Craft (Alchemy) to turn bat guano into explosives. A difficulty 3 craft alchemy roll into 6 charges of firedust. Though it also requires a sprinkling of red jade.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}